Inter-VLAN Routing:
	> End-users in different VLANs are logically in different LANs => Differnt networks => Router is required for inter-vlan communication
	1) Router with sepearate interfaces:
		> Router has an interface in each VLAN as that VLAN's default gateway
		> Advantages/Disadvantages:
			> Requires an interface for each VLAN => Low Scalability
			> Traffic has to go up-down physical ethernet cables => Slow
	2) Router on a stick:
		> Single interface on router and switch is used for all VLANs
		> At the switch, interface is set as a trunk port
		> At the router, interface is split into multiple virtual sub-interfaces, each marked for a VLAN
		> Process:
			> When an end-host sends a frame for its default gateway, frame is sent out the trunk port to the router along with the dot1q tag
			> At router, vlan from dot1q tag is matched against vlans marked on virtual sub-interfaces, frame is made to hit the corresponding virtual sub-interface
		> Advantages/Disadvantages:
			> Less number of router interfaces required => Higher Scalability
			> Traffic has to go up-down single physical ethernet cable => Slow & Higher bandwidth contention
	3) Layer 3 switch:
		> Layer 3 switch: router + switch: an interface is switchport (default), can be configured to routerport => External router
		1) Routing is enabled on the switch -> #ip routing
		2) SVIs (Switched Virtual Interfaces):
			> Virtual interfaces configured on a Layer 3 switch -> #interface vlan 10 // creates a virtual interface, routerport, default gateway for vlan 10
			> Routerports (IP address set on interfaces) // add ip address on SVI
			> Each linked to specific vlan (1-1 relation)
			> Serve as default gateways for respective vlans
			> No manual route configuration required by admin <= all VLANs accessible through connected routes
		4) For routing out of layer 3 switch (eg. to a WAN edge router for external connectivity):
			> Any interface on a layer 3 switch is, by default, switchport, can be configured to a routerport -> #no switchport
			> Add ip address on interface
			> Add a dafult route on layer 3 switch

			
